{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776193876,"nonce":"7GkS4tkRtV4REhH4pDgjDRETdqw=","title":"OpenCode: step_finish:stop should not emit @@DONE@@","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen OpenCode emits `step_finish` with `reason=\"stop\"`, the adapter emits `@@DONE@@`. This is incorrect — `reason=\"stop\"` just means the current model turn finished without tool calls, NOT that the agent completed its task.\n\nThis causes rapid resume loops hitting max-resumes because every model turn triggers a false completion signal.\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_opencode_agent.py::test_parse_step_finish_stop_emits_system\n  Assert: `_parse(step_finish with reason=\"stop\")` returns `AgentEventType.SYSTEM`, not TEXT with @@DONE@@\n- tests/test_opencode_agent.py::test_parse_step_finish_tool_calls\n  Assert: `_parse(step_finish with reason=\"tool-calls\")` returns `AgentEventType.SYSTEM`\n\n## Files\n- adapters/agents/opencode.py (modify)\n- tests/test_opencode_agent.py (modify)\n\n## Implementation\n1. In `_parse()`, remove the special case that emits `@@DONE@@` for `step_finish` with `reason=\"stop\"`\n2. All `step_finish` events should emit `AgentEventType.SYSTEM` with content `step_finish:{reason}`\n3. True completion is signaled by process exit or file signals (`/session/signal/done`)\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee comment in code: \"Note: reason='stop' just means current step finished...\"\n\nREQ: REQ-031","files":null}]}